It uses, and does not change:

- Readium's Go toolkit (https://github.com/readium/go-toolkit), BSD 3-Clause, for EPUB.
- Blitz (https://github.com/DioxusLabs/blitz) with Parley, HarfRust and ICU4X (MIT, Apache License 2.0 or the Unicode
  License), for laying out and drawing pages, and Stylo, Firefox's CSS engine, under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.
- The fonts Parastoo (copyright 2015 Saber Rastikerdar) and Vazirmatn (copyright 2015 The Vazirmatn Project Authors),
  SIL Open Font License 1.1, and DejaVu (copyright 2003 Bitstream, Inc., and the DejaVu changes in the public domain),
  the Bitstream Vera licence: in reader/fonts, each with its licence.

On a Kobo it is started from a row in Kobo's More tab, a launcher of ours inside Kobo's interface whose way in and
row painting are adapted from NickelModManager (https://github.com/nicoverbruggen/NickelModManager, copyright 2026 Nico
Verbruggen, MIT License: its licence is in licenses/LICENSE-NickelModManager.md in the Kobo package, and in
reader/kobo/launcher/LICENSE-NickelModManager.txt).

On a Kindle it is started by a launcher of ours from the Kindle's own library; KOReader
(https://github.com/koreader/koreader, AGPL-3.0) is used only for its SSH server while developing. KOReader is a
separate program and none of its code is copied here.
